// Sortable, printable collections
fn debug_collection[T: Ord + Display + Clone](items: &Vec[T]) {
  let sorted = items.clone();  // Clone
  sorted.sort();               // Ord
  for item in sorted {
    io.println(item.to_str());  // Display
  }
}
```

### Deriving Multiple Interfaces
```xiom
#[derive(Eq, Hash, Clone, Display)]
pub type User = {
  id: Int;
  name: Str;
}

// Now User can be used wherever T: Eq + Hash + Clone + Display is required
```

### Trait Implication
Some constraints imply others. If you have T: Ord, you automatically have T: Eq (because Ord extends Eq). You don't need to write both.

